abstract:
Abstract Corrugated cardboard fly ash (CCFA) is an industrial by-product typically sent to landfill. Unlike conventional coal fly ash, CCFA has limited pozzolanic activity but contains a high amount of calcium oxide (CaO). When hydrated, CaO forms calcium hydroxide (Ca(OH) 2 \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
